ven by the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(3,-4).$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ at $(3,-4):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(3,-4) & =\\frac{3(3)}{(-4)}-3(3)^2(-4) \\\\  & =(- \\frac{9}{4})+(108) \\\\  & =\\frac{423}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["c35d1373-ef75-50e1-b222-ed606ee4a765"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "acd44b37-981b-5c47-acae-e2ba4562ebfc" :answer/id #uuid "acd44b37-981b-5c47-acae-e2ba4562ebfc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{68}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "3399c19f-c144-565d-9a3f-74b3ab3c7fb6" :answer/id #uuid "3399c19f-c144-565d-9a3f-74b3ab3c7fb6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- \\frac{76}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "05407676-cebb-5bc7-a937-477ac92325ff" :answer/id #uuid "05407676-cebb-5bc7-a937-477ac92325ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- \\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "87745150-95ec-582e-a5b6-e67dcf6fbdd9" :answer/id #uuid "87745150-95ec-582e-a5b6-e67dcf6fbdd9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "6a768a59-5859-56ec-9a89-66c3e6901e41" :answer/id #uuid "6a768a59-5859-56ec-9a89-66c3e6901e41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "28" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "bf0d0aa1-5612-5996-9db0-c13d0ba63c6d" :answer-field/id #uuid "bf0d0aa1-5612-5996-9db0-c13d0ba63c6d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["acd44b37-981b-5c47-acae-e2ba4562ebfc" "3399c19f-c144-565d-9a3f-74b3ab3c7fb6" "05407676-cebb-5bc7-a937-477ac92325ff" "87745150-95ec-582e-a5b6-e67dcf6fbdd9" "6a768a59-5859-56ec-9a89-66c3e6901e41"] :answer-field/correct "acd44b37-981b-5c47-acae-e2ba4562ebfc" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "2e5df7a0-85e1-5575-b4c1-bffca0c06fc3" :question/id #uuid "2e5df7a0-85e1-5575-b4c1-bffca0c06fc3" :question/problem "A surface $S$ is defined by $z=f(x,y).$ The curve $C$ is the intersection of $S$ with the plane $x=2.$ Given that the point $P(2,-3,-8)$ lies on $C,$ and that $f_y = \\dfrac{2x}y - 2x^2y$, find the slope of the tangent to $C$ at $P.$" :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $x=2.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve $C$ at the point $P(2,-3,-8)$ will be given by the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(2,-3).$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ at $(2,-3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(2,-3) & =\\frac{2(2)}{(-3)}-2(2)^2(-3) \\\\  & =(- \\frac{4}{3})+(24) \\\\  & =\\frac{68}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["bf0d0aa1-5612-5996-9db0-c13d0ba63c6d"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "86370954-0165-5b77-9084-1afc211cb722" :answer/id #uuid "86370954-0165-5b77-9084-1afc211cb722" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{141}{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "77cc9ca5-7acb-56e5-bc75-c54cce8f4921" :answer/id #uuid "77cc9ca5-7acb-56e5-bc75-c54cce8f4921" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-78" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "72e6360f-cc66-5448-8d12-5f58319b536c" :answer/id #uuid "72e6360f-cc66-5448-8d12-5f58319b536c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-72" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "54085c9b-7316-5f24-9730-29ffe68bc43f" :answer/id #uuid "54085c9b-7316-5f24-9730-29ffe68bc43f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- \\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "256c689b-c454-5525-8358-ac15ab2196c2" :answer/id #uuid "256c689b-c454-5525-8358-ac15ab2196c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- \\frac{147}{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "75ddc911-bb66-5faa-bcc6-bda8bcf585b5" :answer-field/id #uuid "75ddc911-bb66-5faa-bcc6-bda8bcf585b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["86